  "section": "Movie Facts # 5 of 10",
  "description": "Celebrated movie poster illustrator Drew Struzan created the iconic and distinctive images for the ambitious, worldwide Jedi advertising campaign. One artistic decision confused fans. In the film's release poster, Luke Skywalker was heroically depicted holding a blue Lightsaber, even though a blade of that color doesn't appear in the movie itself. Luke's new weapon is green—yet it happens to be blue in one of the early trailers, which suggests that the decision to change the color was taken late in production. The main idea was to make Luke's blade contrast with the blue sky of Tatooine, and enable it to be more visible during the skirmish at Carkoon."
